4. **Keep facts separate from assumptions.**
5. **Do not invent missing information.**
6. **Follow the Revtek brand system.**
7. **Keep the repository modular.**
8. **Avoid unnecessary duplication.**
9. **Preserve existing work.**
10. **Make focused changes.**
11. **Prefer simple, maintainable solutions.**
12. **Document important persistent decisions.**
13. **Keep Claude Code and Codex working from the same source of truth.**
14. **Ask only when missing information materially affects the result.**
15. **When uncertain, make the uncertainty visible.**

